---
description: Prefer design tokens over hardcoded spacing, color, and radius values
alwaysApply: true
---

# Tokens Over Hardcoded Values

When a design token exists, use it. Do not hardcode rem/px/hex that duplicate tokens.

## Prefer

- Spacing: `var(--space-*)`, `var(--layout-gap-*)`, `var(--page-*-gap)`, `var(--card-padding)`, `var(--section-gap)`, `var(--footer-gap)`
- Color: `var(--background)`, `var(--foreground)`, `var(--surface)`, `var(--border)`, `var(--muted)`, `var(--accent)`, …
- In Tailwind arbitrary values: `p-[var(--space-4)]`, `gap-[var(--space-3)]`, `text-[var(--muted)]`

## Allowed hardcoded

- Token **definitions** themselves in `globals.css` (`:root` / `[data-theme]`)
- One-off values with no matching token (document why if non-obvious)
- Third-party / library constraints (e.g. React Grid Layout numeric `margin` that must mirror `--space-4`)

## Do not

- Scatter `p-3`, `gap-4`, `mt-8`, `#181817`, `rgb(...)` on product UI when a token already covers that role
- Invent new magic numbers next to an existing scale step
